{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792744338,"nonce":"WJGamrg0LfC1Byt6HluihushVLs=","title":"Preserve queued native menu actions while menus update","message":"RayDE File \u003e Open Project intermittently needs several clicks. ApplicationMenu.update immediately removed every previous action ID, even though Cocoa could have queued a selection with one of those IDs or could still display that menu while its window was unfocused. pump silently dropped an ID absent from the action map.\n\nA pre-fix Haxe probe captures the Open Project ID, updates the menu, and dispatches that queued ID through the same action map: handler=false, delivered=0. Keep retired handlers through the native queue drain, retain handlers belonging to the currently displayed native payload until it is replaced, and release all handlers when the menu owner closes. Cover window routing, updates during dispatch, bounded cleanup and the native attached picker.","files":null}]}